A||||23||JetroGT||Sealed Berrings?||||5||
Z||000000||JetroGT||12-13-1999||03:26 PM||||<BR>I am getting my rear breaks done along with the berrings. The guy at the break shop tells me that the rear berings are sealed. Is this true? Or is he giving me a line of $#!+?||||reg||5
Z||000001||Cooter||12-13-1999||07:49 PM||||Unless the bearings are noisy or have slack in them, they should not need service. Yes they are a sealed unit that is not serviceable. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||12-13-1999||08:21 PM||||The rear hub unit on all years except 88 is replaced as a whole unit. The hub unit is retained by 3 18mm bolts and a 30mm nut. The hub unit is not servicable.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Eddie||12-13-1999||08:59 PM||||Theorgre I think its they other way around 88,s are hub units and 84 to 87 have berings I think Eddie||||reg||1
Z||000004||GWMORGAN||12-13-1999||09:08 PM||||84-87 are sealed rear hub units.<p>[This message has been edited by GWMORGAN (edited 12-13-1999).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Eddie||12-13-1999||09:18 PM||||are the front and rear hubs the same ? if they are then 84 to 87 you can change the berings I did the front on my 87 two months a go. and I HAD 1988 AND the front berings went. I  had to buy the hub you could not change the berings the hub was 90.00 bucks .||||reg||10
Z||000006||Monkeyman||12-13-1999||10:59 PM||||The front and rear (84-87) are NOT the same.||||reg||1
Z||000007||Standard||12-14-1999||01:26 AM||||the <B>rear</B> bearings are sealed on <B>all</B> years, the <B>front</B> bearings changed to a sealed unit in <B>88</B>||||reg||1
