Z||000018||batboy||12-16-1999||11:31 PM||||Ok guys, lets not beat him up too much, not everyone has the time or the expertise to work on brakes. I remember a time when I was afraid to work on them for fear of messing something up bad. Brakes are pretty important, you know. Yes, you can put vented Grand Am rotors and calipers on the front of non-88 Fieros. Go to my favorite links page on my website, there is a link to a site about the Grand Am swap. If you don't do the rear brakes too, you'll have to use an adjustable proportioning valve. (URL is in my profile). Yes, the "F" word and "G.D." are very harsh cuss words, remember, we have lady members that read this guano.||||reg||1
